; A code invented for something that is not money, declared as a currency.
;
; Loyalty points, air miles, hours — things people do keep in a ledger, and
; the obvious way to write one is to make up a three-letter code for it. A
; currency here is an ISO 4217 currency and nothing else: GnuCash carries that
; table, prices and reports are built on it, and a code no issuer stands
; behind is a security. Which is a namespace away, not a redesign — `PTS.PTS`
; in a namespace of its own does everything this file wanted.
;
; What this fixture produces: an error naming the commodity, and no book.
;
; Verified by tests/integration/test_beancount_reads_what_a_person_writes.py.
2024-01-01 commodity CAD
    gnucash-mnemonic: "CAD"
    gnucash-namespace: "CURRENCY"
    gnucash-fullname: "Canadian Dollar"
    gnucash-fraction: "100"
2024-01-01 commodity PTS
    gnucash-mnemonic: "PTS"
    gnucash-namespace: "CURRENCY"
    gnucash-fullname: "Loyalty Points"
    gnucash-fraction: "1"
